WEBVTT


00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.400
This technique gives a beautiful finish
to the shoulder seams of garments.

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:09.990
Worked in the garment yarn,
or in contrast in colors.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.380
It can add a designer
touch to your next garment.

00:00:15.649 --> 00:00:19.610
Start by binding off your stitches
with a latch tool bind off.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:24.110
You may also know this as a
round-the-gate-peg bind off.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:30.199
Now, if your machine doesn't have gate
pegs or gate posts, you can still work

00:00:30.199 --> 00:00:31.310
this bind off.

00:00:31.729 --> 00:00:36.380
Look for the Knit it Now tutorial
"Stretchy Bind off without Gate Pegs".

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:43.760
You can also find the latch tool bind
off tutorial in the learning library.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:51.900
The idea here is to utilize the chain edge
that's formed with this style of bind off

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:53.490
for our decorative seam.

00:00:55.019 --> 00:01:00.600
Our sample is knit in stockinette, but if
your garment is knit in a stitch pattern,

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:06.750
maybe fair isle or tuck or you've used
short row shaping for the shoulders, be

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:10.800
sure to knitone plain
roll before binding off.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:16.410
Now first align the seams
with the right side facing.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:21.390
You'll pick up the bottom loop
of the bind off from the inside.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:27.120
Join this loop to the corresponding
loop on the other shoulder piece.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.870
Now keep working this way across the row.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:34.620
Pulling the stitches
taught, but not too tight.

00:01:36.225 --> 00:01:40.905
I've used a contrast in color here so you
can see the seaming stitches, the blue

00:01:40.905 --> 00:01:42.045
seaming stitches.

00:01:46.375 --> 00:01:51.115
When you're seaming with the garment yarn
and the seam is neat and tidy and it forms

00:01:51.115 --> 00:01:54.384
a decorative Ridge on the
public side of the work.

00:01:54.804 --> 00:01:58.315
To summarize, knit one row plain.

00:01:59.884 --> 00:02:04.725
Bind off each of your shoulder
pieces around the gate pegs.

00:02:05.975 --> 00:02:08.014
With the right side facing.

00:02:08.164 --> 00:02:14.885
Pick up the inside loops of the bind off
stitches and join the seam all the way

00:02:14.885 --> 00:02:15.725
across.

00:02:17.815 --> 00:02:20.995
Pull your seeming thread taught.

00:02:21.825 --> 00:02:25.315
But not tight and block your seam.

00:02:26.955 --> 00:02:29.325
Don't try to hide your shoulder seams.

00:02:29.745 --> 00:02:30.945
Show them off.

00:02:31.965 --> 00:02:33.525
Thank you for watching.

00:02:34.575 --> 00:02:39.585
If you'd like to see the other seaming
techniques available in the learning

00:02:39.585 --> 00:02:44.235
library, please consider a
subscription to Knit it Now.

00:02:45.475 --> 00:02:50.665
You'll have full access to all the
tutorials and many other benefits.

00:02:52.345 --> 00:02:53.155
Happy knitting.

